{"name":"Twinkle Toes","hex":"#e2d39b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twinkle toes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone with extraordinary footwork."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twinkle_toes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twinkle Toes","blocks":[{"text":"Twinkle Toes is the largest excavator in the Southern Hemisphere. It was used in Christchurch to demolish tall buildings following the 2010 and 2011 earthquakes before moving to Wellington following the 2016 Kaikōura earthquake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/PWC_building_demolition_09.JPG/330px-PWC_building_demolition_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twinkle_Toes","wikidata":"Q7858388"},{"title":"Toe","blocks":[{"text":"Toes are the digits of the foot of a tetrapod. Animal species such as cats that walk on their toes are described as being digitigrade. Humans, and other animals that walk on the soles of their feet, are described as being plantigrade; unguligrade animals are those that walk on hooves at the tips of their toes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Toes.png/330px-Toes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toe","wikidata":"Q154425"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liverpool_Street_06.jpg/500px-Liverpool_Street_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liverpool_Street_06.jpg/1280px-Liverpool_Street_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Liverpool_Street_06.jpg/500px-Liverpool_Street_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Twinkle Toes' fir