arsal bone, which is mildly broadened distally. The duplicated toes have almost normal growth. The fifth toe has mild varus angulation, and the sixth toe has substantial valgus angulation.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AX-ray_of_feet_in_polydactyly.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Metti_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Metti_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Metti_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Metti_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman's toes decorated with nail polish and henna, and wearing a metti (toe ring) on the second toe, for her wedding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMetti_(cropped).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Red_Pink_Orange_rainbow_toesocks.jpg/500px-Red_Pink_Orange_rainbow_toesocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Red_Pink_Orange_rainbow_toesocks.jpg/500px-Red_Pink_Orange_rainbow_toesocks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Striped toe socks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Pink_Orange_rainbow_toesocks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/EnPointeFoot.jpg/500px-EnPointeFoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/EnPointeFoot.jpg/500px-EnPointeFoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"En pointe foot in a pointe shoe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnPointeFoot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/PaluchUStopy.jpg/500px-PaluchUStopy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam